<title>NETHERLANDS: Heidemij sees higher 1997 net.</title>
<headline>Heidemij sees higher 1997 net.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch engineering consultancy Heidemij said on Tuesday it expected a clear increase in net results from ordinary operations over the full 1997 year.  </p>
<p>&quot;Within the framework of current market trends and with the addition of the activities of Geotecnica Consultores and Articon we expect a further growth in sales and a clear growth in the net result before extraordinary gains in 1997,&quot; the group said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The company earlier announced first-half net profits rose to 24.8 million guilders from a year-earlier 12.4 million. This included an extraordinary gain of 11.1 million guilders in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
